---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '@easy-web/core/components/Section.astro';
import Prose from '@easy-web/core/components/Prose.astro';
import Card from '@easy-web/core/components/Card.astro';
import CardGrid from '@easy-web/core/components/CardGrid.astro';
import { base, href } from '../../lib/showcase';

// The technology map lives on the docs site, which is deployed beside the showcase.
const technologyMap = `${base}docs/architecture/technology-map/`;
---

<Base
  title="Getting Started — easy-web"
  lang="en"
  description="Learn how to set up your first easy-web project in 5 minutes."
>
  <article class="guide">
    <Prose>
      <h1>Getting Started with easy-web</h1>
      <p class="lead">Set up your first easy-web project in 5 minutes.</p>

      <h2 id="prerequisites">1. Prerequisites</h2>
      <p>Before you begin, make sure you have the following installed on your machine:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Node.js 24 and pnpm 10 (recommended)</li>
        <li>An Astro 7 project (or create a new one)</li>
        <li>Existing sites can stay on Node.js 22 with Astro 6, which remains supported. The <a href={technologyMap}>technology map</a> shows what each package is validated on.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Node.js only builds your site. The result is static, so nothing needs Node.js to serve it.</p>
      <p>Verify your installation by running these commands in your terminal:</p>
      <pre><code>node --version
pnpm --version</code></pre>
      <p>If you need to start from scratch, run:</p>
      <pre><code>pnpm create astro@latest my-site</code></pre>

      <h2 id="install">2. Install Packages</h2>
      <p>Install the easy-web core package to your project. It provides design tokens, i18n helpers, and UI components.</p>
      <pre><code>pnpm add @easy-web/core</code></pre>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>styles</strong> and <strong>theme</strong>: CSS variables, dark mode logic, and typography.</li>
        <li><strong>i18n</strong>: Bilingual routing and translation utilities.</li>
        <li><strong>components</strong>: Accessible, themed Astro components.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="tokens">3. Add Design Tokens</h2>
      <p>Import the global design tokens in your main layout file and include the <code>noFlashScript</code> to prevent dark mode flickering during page load.</p>
      <pre><code>// Import tokens
import '@easy-web/core/styles/tokens.css';
import &#123; noFlashScript &#125; from '@easy-web/core/theme';

&lt;html&gt;
  &lt;head&gt;
    &lt;script is:inline set:html=&#123;noFlashScript&#125;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;/head&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>

      <h2 id="components">4. Use Components</h2>
      <p>Start building your pages using the provided content blocks. These components automatically use your theme tokens.</p>
      <pre><code>// Use components
import Hero from '@easy-web/core/components/Hero.astro';
import ThemeToggle from '@easy-web/core/components/ThemeToggle.astro';

&lt;Hero
  title="My Site"
  subtitle="Built with easy-web"
  ctaLabel="Learn More"
  ctaHref="/about"
/&gt;
&lt;ThemeToggle /&gt;</code></pre>
    </Prose>

    <Section title="5. Next Steps" id="next-steps">
      <p>Now that you're set up, explore the rest of the ecosystem to build even faster.</p>
      <CardGrid>
        <Card
          item={{
            title: 'Component Gallery',
            description: 'Browse all available UI blocks and their variations.',
            href: href('en', 'components/'),
          }}
        />
        <Card
          item={{
            title: 'Theme Gallery',
            description: 'See how different design systems look on the same components.',
            href: `${base}themes/`,
          }}
        />
        <Card
          item={{
            title: 'API Documentation',
            description: 'Deep dive into the props and internals of each package.',
            href: `${base}docs/`,
          }}
        />
      </CardGrid>
    </Section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Keeps the next-steps cards in the same column as the Prose text above them:
     the 45rem reading column plus the side padding Prose and Section both add. */
  .guide {
    max-width: calc(45rem + 2 * var(--ew-space-5));
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--ew-text-lg);
  }
  /* The sticky header would otherwise cover a heading reached through its anchor. */
  h2[id] {
    scroll-margin-top: var(--ew-space-9);
  }
  strong {
    color: var(--ew-primary);
  }
</style>
